.TH CTable n 28/07/98 "CADC"
.\".BS
.SH NAME
CTable
\- Create and manipulate a CTable widget.

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBCTable\fI \fIpathName \fR?\fIoptions\fR?

.SH "INHERITANCE"
itk::Widget \<- iwidgets::LabeledWidget \<- iwidgets::Scrolledframe \<- CTable

.SO
\-activebackground	\-font			\-relief
\-activerelief	\-foreground		\-repeatdelay
\-background	\-highlightcolor	\-repeatinterval
\-borderwidth	\-highlightthickness	\-selectbackground
\-cursor	\-jump			\-troughcolor
.SE

.SH "INHERITED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-clientdata\fR	\fB\-labelfont\fR	\fB\-labelvariable\fR
\fB\-elementborderwidth\fR	\fB\-labelimage\fR	\fB\-sbwidth\fR
\fB\-height\fR		\fB\-labelmargin\fR	\fB\-scrollmargin\fR
\fB\-hscrollmode\fR	\fB\-labelpos\fR	\fB\-vscrollmode\fR
\fB\-labelbitmap\fR	\fB\-labeltext\fR	\fB\-width\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBiwidgets::Scrolledframe\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"

.OP \-cellbd cellBorderWidth BorderWidth
Specifies the width of the three dimensional border around each of the
cells in the table.  The default value is 0.

.OP \-columnwidths columnWidths ColumnWidths
Specifies the width of each column in pixels.  

.OP \-headings headings Headings
Specifies the text that appears above each column.

.OP \-tablefont tableFont Font
Specifies the font to use when drawing text inside the
table portion.
.\".BE

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBCTable\fR command creates a new window (given by the
\fIpathName\fR argument) and makes it into a CTable widget.
Additional options, described above, may be specified on the 
command line or in the option database to configure aspects of
the table. The \fBCTable\fR command returns its
\fIpathName\fR argument.  At the time this command is invoked,
there must not exist a window named \fIpathName\fR, but
\fIpathName\fR's parent must exist.
.PP
The \fBCTable\fR command creates a table widget 
capable of adding, inserting, deleting, rows and cells of data into
a table.


.SH "INHERITED COMMANDS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBchildsite\fR	\fBxview\fR	\fByview\fR
\fBjustify\fR	
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBiwdigets::Scrolledframe\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited commands

.SH "WINDGET COMMAND"
The \fBCTable\fR command creates a new Tcl command whose
name is \fIpathName\fR.  This
command may be used to invoke various
operations on the widget.  It has the following general form:
.CS
\fIpathName method \fR?\fIarg arg ...\fR?
.CE
\fIMethod\fR and the \fIarg\fRs
determine the exact behavior of the command.  
.PP
Many of the widget methods (commands) for the \fBCTable\fR take one or
two position arguments.
The position arguments inform the \fBCTable\fR method which
row or cell to operate on.  These positions
are called \fIrow indexes\fR and \fIcolumn indexes\fR.  They allow 
specific cells and rows to be referenced
and manipulated.
The row and column indexes may be specified in a numeric form only, except
\fIend\fR which is a valid index.  
.TP 12
\fInumber\fR
Specifies the column or row  numerically, where 0 corresponds to the top 
row for a row index and to the left most column for a column index.
.TP 12
\fIend\fR 
Specifies the last row or column.

.PP
The following methods are possible for CTable widgets:

.TP
\fIpathName \fBaddCell\fR \fIrow\fR \fIvalue\fR
Adds a cell after the last cell in the row specified by
\fIrow\fR.  The \fIvalue\fR is inserted into this cell.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBaddRow\fR \fIvalues\fR
Adds a row after the last row in the table.
The \fIvalues\fR are inserted into the cells of this row The
first item in the value list is inserted in the first cell.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcget\fR \fIoption\fR
Returns the current value of the configuration option given
by \fIoption\fR.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCTable\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcomponent\fR ?\fIname\fR? ?\fIcommand arg arg ...\fR?
Used to query or access component widgets within the CTable
widget.  For example the \fIheadings\fR are a component of
the \fBCTable\fR widget.  With no arguments, this method returns a list 
of symbolic names for component widgets that are accessible in the
current scope.  
.sp
If a symbolic \fIname\fR is specified this method returns the window
path name for that component.
.sp
Otherwise, the \fIcommand\fR and any remaining \fIarg\fR arguments
are invoked as a method on the component with the symbolic \fIname\fR.
This provides a well-defined mechanism for accessing internal components
without relying on specific window path names.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBconfig\fR
See \fBconfigure\fI.

.TP
\fIpathName\fR \fBconfigure\fR ?\fIoption\fR? ?\fIvalue option value ...\fR?
Query or modify the configuration options of the widget.
If no \fIoption\fR is specified, returns a list describing all of
the available options for \fIpathName\fR (see \fBTk_ConfigureInfo\fR for
information on the format of this list).  If \fIoption\fR is specified
with no \fIvalue\fR, then the command returns a list describing the
one named option (this list will be identical to the corresponding
sublist of the value returned if no \fIoption\fR is specified).  If
one or more \fIoption\-value\fR pairs are specified, then the command
modifies the given widget option(s) to have the given value(s);  in
this case the command returns an empty string.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCTable\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBdeleteCell\fR \fIrow column\fR
Deletes (removes) a specified cell from the table, given by \fIrow\fR
and \fIcolumn\fR.  All cells positioned to the right of the deleted
cell will be shifted to the left by one cell.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBdeleteRow\fR \fIrow\fR
Deletes (removes) a specified row from the table, given by \fIrow\fR.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBgetCell\fR \fIrow column\fR
Returns the contents of a cell in the table, given by \fIrow\fR
and \fIcolumn\fR.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBgetCellPath\fR \fIrow column\fR
Returns the window path name of a cell in the table, given by \fIrow\fR
and \fIcolumn\fR.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBgetRow\fR \fIrow\fR
Returns the contents of a row in the table, given by \fIrow\fR.
The return value is a list where the first item is the contents of
the first (leftmost) cell in the row.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBgetRowPath\fR \fIrow\fR
Returns the window path name of a row in the table, given by \fIrow\fR.


.TP
\fIpathName \fBinsertCell\fR \fIrow column value\fR
Inserts a cell before the cell specified by \fIrow\fR and \fIcolumn\fR.
The contents of the cell will be the value given. 

.TP
\fIpathName \fBinsertRow\fR \fIrow values\fR
Inserts a cell before the cell specified by \fIrow\fR.  The \fIvalues\fR
are a list of values, one for each cell in the row. The first item in 
the \fIvalues\fR list
is inserted into the first (leftmost) cell. 

.TP
\fIpathName \fBisa\fR \fIclassName\fR
Sets the class of the \fBCTable\fR object to the specified class name.
 
.TP
\fIpathName \fBselectRow\fR \fIrow\fR
Selects, highlights, the given row.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBselectedRow\fR
Returns the numerical row index of the selected row.  The topmost row
has an index of 0.  If no row is selected then \-1 is returned.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBsetCell\fR \fIrow column value\fR
Changes or sets the value of a cell, given by \fIrow\fR and 
\fIcolumn\fR, to the value given.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBsetRow\fR \fIrow values\fR
Changes or sets the values of a row, given by \fIrow\fR,
to the values given. \fIvalues\fR is a list of values, typically
one for each cell in the row.  The first item in the \fIvalues\fR list
is inserted into the first (leftmost) cell.

.SH "COMPONENTS"
.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBheadFrame\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
The heading frame component provides "relief" for the area where the
headings are displayed.
See the \fBframe\fR widget manual entry for details on the
headFrame component.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBheadCanvas\fR
Class:  \fBcanvas\fR
.fi
.IP
The heading canvas component provides scrolling to the
heading region.  See the "canvas" widget manual
entry for details on the headCanvas component item.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBheadings\fR
Class:  \fBframe\fR
.fi
.IP
The headings component is where the headings are displayed.
See the \fBframe\fR widget manual entry for details on the
headings component.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBheadMargin\fR
Class:  \fBframe\fR
.fi
.IP
The headings margin is the component which provides spacing
between the headings and the table.
See the \fBframe\fR widget manual entry for details on the
headMargin component.

.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
.PP
The CTable widget generally has the same bindings as its inherited
widget, \fBscrolledframe\fR.  However, it also adds one binding:
.PP
[1] Button-1 mouse press over any of the entries on the table 
causes the row to be highlighted (selected).

.SH EXAMPLE
.DS
 CTable .t -labeltext "Test Table" -width 300 -height 300
 .t configure  -headings { "heading 1" "heading 2" "heading 3"} 
 .t addRow  { 1 2 3 }
 .t insertRow 0 { 4 5 6 }
 .t insertRow  1 { 7 8 9 }
 .t addRow { 10 11 12 }
 .t addRow { 13 14 15 }
 .t deleteRow 2
 .t insertRow 0 { 1 2 3 } 
 .t config -columnwidths { 10 10 15 } -cellbd 2

 pack .t -fill both -expand yes
.DE

.SH BUGS
Not all functionality is implemented yet. In particular the \fIaddCell\fR,
\fIdeleteCell\fR, and \fIinsertCell\fR widget commands.

.SH AUTHOR
Shannon Jaeger

.SH KEYWORDS
CTable, table, widget
